Operator --> PREPRESS
Source --> IMPORT
Resources --> CHECK
Operator --> PREVIEW
Operator --> RESOLVE
Operator --> PDF
Operator --> PRINT

PREPRESS ..> IMPORT : <<include>>
PREPRESS ..> ASSEMBLE : <<include>>
PREPRESS ..> GEOMETRY : <<include>>
PREPRESS ..> IMPOSE : <<include>>
PREPRESS ..> PREFLIGHT : <<include>>
PREPRESS ..> PREVIEW : <<include>>

EDIT ..> ASSEMBLE : <<extend>>
MARKUP ..> ASSEMBLE : <<extend>>
PREFLIGHT ..> CHECK : <<include>>
RESOLVE ..> PREFLIGHT : <<extend>>

PDF ..> PREPRESS : <<extend>>
PRINT ..> PREPRESS : <<extend>>
PRINT ..> SELECT : <<include>>
PRINT ..> OPTIONS : <<include>>
PRINT ..> BATCH : <<include>>
SELECT --> Destination
PRINT --> Destination
Destination --> Printer

note bottom of PREPRESS
  Compound-document assembly is a shared capability.
  The pre-press outcome is distinguished by output intent,
  preflight, imposition, and destination compatibility.
end note
@enduml
